# ClinicMaxx — local environment
#
# This file is gitignored (.env*.local). Never commit it, never paste its
# contents into a chat window or an issue.
#
# Where to find these:
#   Supabase dashboard -> your project -> Connect (top bar) -> "ORMs" tab
#   Replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with the database password you set when you created
#   the project. If you've lost it: Settings -> Database -> Reset database password.
#
# If a password contains @ : / ? # or & it must be percent-encoded, because it
# sits inside a URL. @ becomes %40, # becomes %23, / becomes %2F.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. DATABASE_URL — what the running app uses for every page load.
#
# Use the TRANSACTION POOLER, port 6543. It is built for short-lived
# serverless-style connections, which is exactly what a Next.js server
# component does. It is also IPv4-reachable, unlike the direct connection.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. MIGRATION_URL — used only by `npm run db:migrate` and `npm run db:push`.
#
# Use the SESSION POOLER, port 5432. Creating tables and bulk-loading needs
# session state and prepared statements that transaction mode does not keep.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
MIGRATION_URL=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Not needed for the migration — the app talks straight to Postgres.
# Only fill these in if you later add Supabase Auth, Storage or Realtime.
#
# The anon key is safe to expose in a browser ONLY because every table has Row
# Level Security enabled with no policies. Do not add permissive policies
# without thinking about who can then read the clinical record.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Server-only. Bypasses RLS entirely. Never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
